f evolution preserved: a comprehensive catalog of the processed pseudogenes in the human genome.</article-title><source>Genome Res</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>2541</fpage><lpage>58</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14656962</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005040-Pavlicek1"><label>6</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pavlicek</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gentles</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Paces</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Paces</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Jurka</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Retroposition of processed pseudogenes: the impact of RNA stability and translational control.</article-title><source>Trends Genet</source><volume>22</volume><fpage>69</fpage><lpage>73</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16356584</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005040-Kaessmann1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaessmann</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Vinckenbosch</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Long</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2009</year><article-title>RNA-based gene duplication: mechanistic and evolutionary insights.</article-title><source>NATURE REVIEWS GENETICS</source><volume>10</volume><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>31</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005040-Robinson1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Retrocopied genes may enhance male fitness.</article-title><source>Plos biology</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>e399</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005040-Betran1"><label>9<